69 single-token mutants of `server/jobs_retry.py` were run against this file alone, stopping at each mutant's first failing test: comparison, boolean, return, offset, operator swaps, integer-literal swaps including the literals 0 and 1, and the arithmetic swaps `-`/`+`, `*`/`//`, `*`/`-`, `**`/`*`, `%`/`//`. Comment and docstring text is not mutated. 66 are killed by semantic outcomes (an assertion, an oracle mismatch or a wrong typed class). 2 are crash-only and are not counted as kills: `operations[1]` and `operations[2]` in the contract loader raise IndexError at import time, so no test runs. The 1 survivor, `ensure_ascii=True` to `False` in the canonical encoder, is behavior-equivalent: every string the digest covers is ASCII by grammar or enum.
